title: user:tag-add
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Customising the GUI]]
kind: reference
summary: Add a tag to the selected metarecord

`user:tag-add <tag|negative_tag|mixed_tag> <tag>` gives the selected metarecord a tag, denies it, or marks it mixed, the field naming the answer: it runs [[mf:tag]] `add`, `deny` or `mixed`, so the rules of [[Tag subsumption]] hold, and a path that names no tag yet creates it. The completion offers the paths of the existing tags. The keys are `# a t`, `# a n` and `# a m` ([[Tagging from the GUI]]). An example of the shipped `commands.js`, to edit or delete ([[User commands]]).
